  "body": "Hi,\n\nI noticed an issue with RAW support for the Nikon Zf (and probably every modern nikon camera as well)\n\n<img width=\"1819\" height=\"978\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cce6f272-33c4-4b2e-95e7-400e3320a651\" />\n\nThe camera offers three NEF compression options:\n- Lossless compression → works correctly\n- High Efficiency (*) → not working properly\n- High Efficiency → not working properly\n\nObserved behavior:\n\nART:\n- Files can be opened\n- However, the image is rendered with completely incorrect / corrupted colors\n\nRawTherapee:\n- Files cannot be processed\n- The application crashes when attempting to open these files\n\nDetails:\n- Camera: Nikon Zf\n- File types: NEF (High Efficiency and High Efficiency *)\n- RawTherapee version: 5.12\n- ART version: 1.26.3\n- OS: Open Suse Tumbleweed\n\nThe same files work correctly in:\n- Nikon NX Studio\n- Adobe Lightroom\n\nI have sample RAW files for all three compression types (lossless, HE, HE*) and can provide them if needed.\n\nThis might be related to missing or incomplete support in LibRaw for the newer Nikon compression formats, but I wanted to report it here first in case there is anything that can be handled on this side.\n\nLet me know if further testing or files would help.\n\nThanks!",
